---
# yamllint disable rule:line-length
# Lifts the user's own `boxed()` into a `Φ.hone.box`, and MARKS it `user ↦
# Φ.true` — the one box in the pipeline that is the caller's element type and
# not scaffolding. `208-mapToObj`, `211` and `214` mint boxes of their own, and
# `221-unbox-box-to-map` cancels an unbox against whatever box follows it, so
# without the mark it cannot tell the two apart. It could not before, either,
# and that was #1016: a primitive `distinct()` or `skip(n)` with a `boxed()`
# right behind it ends `214`'s sandwich in an unbox, `221` cancelled that unbox
# against the user's box and kept only the unbox, and the boxing the user asked
# for was gone — `501` then lowered the run to `mapMultiToInt` while the caller
# held the `Stream` `boxed()` had promised, and the first element threw
# `IncompatibleClassChangeError`.
#
# The mark is on THIS box rather than on the three synthetic ones because every
# other rule that reads a box — `209`, `411`, the two `443-unsandwich` rules,
# `602` — wants all of them, and a closed pattern with an extra binding in it
# stops matching. They carry a trailing `𝐵-box-rest` for that reason and go on
# seeing exactly what they saw before; only `221` discriminates.
name: boxed-to-box
pattern: |
  ⟦
    φ ↦ Φ.jeo.opcode.invokeinterface,
    𝜏-target-stream-class ↦ 𝑒-target-stream-class,
    𝜏-method ↦ "boxed",
    𝜏-result-stream-class ↦ "()Ljava/util/stream/Stream;",
    𝜏-flag ↦ Φ.true,
    ρ ↦ ∅
  ⟧
result: |
  ⟦
    φ ↦ Φ.hone.box,
    stream-class ↦ 𝑒-target-stream-class,
    user ↦ Φ.true
  ⟧
when:
  or:
    - eq: [𝑒-target-stream-class, '"java/util/stream/IntStream"']
    - eq: [𝑒-target-stream-class, '"java/util/stream/LongStream"']
    - eq: [𝑒-target-stream-class, '"java/util/stream/DoubleStream"']
